<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco lifts bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco lifts bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has lifted A-960 bunker fuel prices from Ras Tanura and Dammam by 50 cents to $105 a tonne ($16.12 a barrel) with effect May 22, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-960 bunker fuel oil from the Red Sea ports of Jeddah and Yanbu climbed by $2 to $100 a tonne ($15.35 a barrel).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the two Gulf ports is 50 cents higher at $212 a tonne and $1.5 higher from the Red Sea at $198.5 a tonne.</p>
</text>
